*** DEPRECATED >> Object.finalize() - deprecated since Java 9, marked "forRemoval=true" since Java 18
    >> the example above uses finalize() - IMPORTANT to know this method itself is deprecated for removal
    >> reason - finalize() timing is unpredictable, hurts GC performance, can resurrect objects, security risks
    >> use instead >> java.lang.ref.Cleaner (Java 9+) or try-with-resources / AutoCloseable for cleanup logic
    >> so beyond the access-modifier override error shown above, overriding finalize() at all is discouraged in Java 17

